WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:05.040
Leadership, going forward,
is only going to be great

00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:08.440
if women are at 50%.

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:11.680
Hi, I'm Sally Helgeson.

00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:13.200
I'm an author, speaker

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:15.440
and leadership development consultant

00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:17.440
and I work all over the world.

00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:21.840
Here I'm going to talk about
five of those behaviours

00:00:21.920 --> 00:00:24.320
that most commonly
get in women's ways.

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:28.560
The first behaviour is a reluctance
to claim your achievements.

00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:31.920
Expecting others
to spontaneously notice

00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:36.000
and reward your contributions
and your hard work.

00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:38.640
When I do workshops
now I often ask,

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:41.800
"How good are you at bringing
attention to your work?"

00:00:42.040 --> 00:00:45.280
And what I often hear is,
"I'm not good at that at all."

00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:48.560
And when I ask them,
"Why aren't you good?"

00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:50.320
I hear one of two responses.

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:53.840
The first is, "I would think
that if I do good work

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:55.680
people should notice."

00:00:55.760 --> 00:00:58.720
They probably should
but I don't think it's gonna happen

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:00.320
in today's workplace.

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:01.800
The other thing I hear is,

00:01:01.880 --> 00:01:06.080
"If I have to act like that obnoxious
jerk down the hall to get noticed,

00:01:06.160 --> 00:01:07.640
I'd rather not get noticed."

00:01:07.720 --> 00:01:11.640
And that's problematic because it
behaves an either/or way of thinking

00:01:11.720 --> 00:01:13.680
that is going to get in your way.

00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:16.400
If you set yourself up
either you're obnoxious

00:01:16.480 --> 00:01:18.600
and constantly talking
about yourself,

00:01:18.680 --> 00:01:21.640
or you just hang back
and hope others notice.

00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:24.360
You've got a kind of
no win place to be.

00:01:25.240 --> 00:01:27.560
For example, you might identify,

00:01:27.640 --> 00:01:31.760
"You know, I think that my boss
doesn't really understand

00:01:31.840 --> 00:01:35.880
how well connected
I am in this organisation.

00:01:36.280 --> 00:01:38.840
So I think what I'm going to do

00:01:38.920 --> 00:01:42.520
is once a week I'm going to
shoot him a quick email

00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:44.120
that just summarises

00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:47.560
the main people that
I've managed to talk to that week."

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:51.720
I have seen this be remarkably
successful for women.

00:01:52.600 --> 00:01:56.000
The second behaviour
is the disease to please.

00:01:56.080 --> 00:02:00.120
That is hoping
and wanting everyone to think

00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:03.240
you are a wonderful
and always nice person.

00:02:03.640 --> 00:02:05.920
Now this is a typical behaviour

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:08.920
that can be very helpful
early in your career

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:13.040
but can really get in your way
as you seek to rise.

00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:14.760
Why is that true?

00:02:14.840 --> 00:02:17.400
First of all, if you're
always seeking to please

00:02:17.480 --> 00:02:21.440
you're going to have a hard time
holding other people accountable

00:02:21.520 --> 00:02:23.840
for showing up
for what they've promised

00:02:23.920 --> 00:02:27.720
because you're going to be afraid
that maybe they won't like you.

00:02:27.800 --> 00:02:29.880
You're going to have a hard time
saying no to things

00:02:29.960 --> 00:02:32.360
and end up saying yes too often

00:02:32.440 --> 00:02:35.840
and you're going to
let people who will take advantage,

00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:39.520
violate your own
boundaries and waste a lot of time.

00:02:39.880 --> 00:02:43.400
I'm not saying here that you don't
want to be a wonderful person

00:02:43.480 --> 00:02:47.960
but being invested in everyone
thinking you're wonderful and nice

00:02:48.040 --> 00:02:51.560
is, if you seek to rise,
going to get in your way.

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:54.680
If you can start small

00:02:54.760 --> 00:02:58.240
again by asserting boundaries
in one way

00:02:58.320 --> 00:03:01.880
say to yourself,
"Right now I'm over committed

00:03:02.520 --> 00:03:04.400
so that in the next month

00:03:04.760 --> 00:03:10.120
when people ask me to join
a new taskforce or something else

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:14.080
I'm going to think about it
very deliberately before I say yes.

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:18.280
And I'm not only going to think about
how would it please them,

00:03:18.360 --> 00:03:21.200
but I'm going to think about,
"How might it serve me?

00:03:21.280 --> 00:03:23.680
Is this really in my best interests?"

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:29.520
A third behaviour that often gets
in women's way is perfectionism.

00:03:29.600 --> 00:03:34.200
Trying to put so much energy
into doing everything right

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:37.400
that you can't see
the forest for the trees

00:03:37.480 --> 00:03:42.400
and you waste a lot of time trying to
make improvements at the margins

00:03:42.480 --> 00:03:46.640
that aren't going to necessarily
position you to move higher.

00:03:46.720 --> 00:03:50.160
One big problem
with being a perfectionist

00:03:50.240 --> 00:03:54.720
is that you'll have trouble
delegating work to other people

00:03:54.800 --> 00:03:57.960
because you're so invested
in it being perfect

00:03:58.040 --> 00:04:00.720
you're going to be afraid
that they'll make mistakes.

00:04:00.800 --> 00:04:03.000
So you'll end up doing, often,

00:04:03.080 --> 00:04:06.440
a lot of work
of other people's, yourself.

00:04:06.520 --> 00:04:08.520
And I often hear perfectionists say

00:04:08.600 --> 00:04:11.200
"Oh it's just easier
to do everything myself."

00:04:11.640 --> 00:04:13.960
Now again, you want
to start small here.

00:04:14.040 --> 00:04:16.880
You might just want
to identify one person

00:04:16.960 --> 00:04:20.040
who you're going to decide
to delegate to,

00:04:20.120 --> 00:04:23.480
give them an opportunity,
offer them feedback

00:04:23.560 --> 00:04:27.480
but don't stay on top of it
and take that risk.

00:04:27.560 --> 00:04:29.960
One of the things
that's really interesting

00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:32.200
is that studies show that

00:04:32.280 --> 00:04:35.640
women in organisations
tend to be more rewarded

00:04:35.720 --> 00:04:38.320
for being precise and correct,

00:04:38.400 --> 00:04:42.360
whereas men in organisations
tend to be rewarded

00:04:42.440 --> 00:04:45.040
more for risk-taking and boldness.

00:04:45.120 --> 00:04:46.680
So as you seek to rise

00:04:46.760 --> 00:04:49.520
you want to learn to take risks

00:04:49.600 --> 00:04:55.800
and move away from being
overly precise and perfectionistic.

00:04:56.200 --> 00:05:01.400
The fourth behaviour is ruminating
over the mistakes you've made.

00:05:01.480 --> 00:05:03.800
This can really keep you stuck,

00:05:04.520 --> 00:05:07.640
and it's much more common
in women than men.

00:05:07.720 --> 00:05:10.480
Research has shown that rumination

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:15.680
is much more likely to be
a behavioural impediment for women.

00:05:16.960 --> 00:05:19.200
It's a form of beating yourself up.

00:05:19.280 --> 00:05:24.480
Rather than letting mistakes go
and figuring you're a human being

00:05:24.560 --> 00:05:27.440
and you will make mistakes
like everyone else.

00:05:28.400 --> 00:05:30.720
Finally, minimising.

00:05:30.800 --> 00:05:35.480
Either in terms of speech
or minimising in terms of

00:05:35.560 --> 00:05:39.320
how you hold your physical self
in the world.

00:05:39.400 --> 00:05:42.680
Women can be
reluctant to hold their space.

00:05:43.280 --> 00:05:48.080
That is, shrinking their body at
times or not really standing up

00:05:48.160 --> 00:05:51.040
with authority as if they
belong where they are

00:05:51.120 --> 00:05:53.720
especially when they're
at higher echelons

00:05:53.800 --> 00:05:56.760
or trying to position themselves
as a leader.

00:05:56.840 --> 00:06:00.120
Women often will also
use minimising phrases

00:06:00.200 --> 00:06:03.040
in their speech -
"Oh, do you just have one minute?"

00:06:03.400 --> 00:06:05.040
"Can I only make one point?"

00:06:05.120 --> 00:06:06.720
And of course, our old favourite,

00:06:06.800 --> 00:06:10.400
apologising is a form
of minimising yourself.

00:06:11.680 --> 00:06:13.120
So what you want to do

00:06:13.440 --> 00:06:16.320
if you're trying to
position yourself as a leader

00:06:16.400 --> 00:06:18.360
is to hold your space

00:06:18.440 --> 00:06:24.720
and show up as if you know that
you are worthy, whole and complete.

00:06:26.960 --> 00:06:28.200
But I want to point out

00:06:28.280 --> 00:06:31.040
that I've been doing a lot of
interviews and a lot of events

00:06:31.120 --> 00:06:34.760
and I can't tell you how many times
people have said

00:06:34.840 --> 00:06:36.120
- men have said to me -

00:06:36.200 --> 00:06:39.120
"I really identify with
some of these behaviours."

00:06:39.200 --> 00:06:42.920
And that speaks to, I think,
a greater commonality

00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:46.280
between women and men
that is one of the real forces

00:06:46.360 --> 00:06:49.880
that is driving and
changing the workplace.

00:06:54.740 --> 00:07:00.120
Thanks for watching. 
Don’t forget to subscribe! :)

